cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DaiDocs or report its scores, please cite as below and state the method version, the answering model, the judge snapshot and the denominator of the run."
title: "DaiDocs: Plain-Text AI-Native Memory"
version: V4.4n32
authors:
  - family-names: Rigi
    given-names: Amin
    email: amin@daidocs.com
  - family-names: Munir
    given-names: Muhammad Ali
    email: ali@daidocs.com
  - name: "The DaiDocs contributors"
year: 2026
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kerneta/daidocs"
url: "https://daidocs.com"
abstract: >
  DaiDocs (.dai) is a plain-text memory layer for language models: three-zone
  documents plus a derived index, written once by an observer model and read by
  any answering model. On LongMemEval-S, all 500 questions, scored by the
  benchmark authors' own evaluate_qa.py with judge snapshot gpt-4o-2024-08-06,
  the daidocs-v44n engine scores 83.00% with GPT-4o answering and 92.00% with
  Claude Fable 5 over the identical store. Accuracy is not model-independent:
  the same store spans 14 points across five answering models, so any score
  quoted without naming its actor is incomplete. Conditions and disclosures are
  in docs/RESULTS.md.
